<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Rogue Amoeba opened its doors on September 30, 2002, and they&#8217;re celebrating 24 years with a birthday sale: 24% off anything in <a href="https://rogueamoeba.com/store/">their store</a> with the code <strong>24YEARS</strong>. The discount runs through October 4.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I use Rogue Amoeba apps every day. Audio Hijack, Fission, and SoundSource are baked into how I record every podcast. My wife, who is very much not a power user, loves Piezo. If you&#8217;ve been eyeing one of their apps (or the upgrade to SoundSource 6), this is the week to do it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The latest versions of their whole lineup also <a href="https://weblog.rogueamoeba.com/2026/09/11/all-rogue-amoeba-apps-support-the-new-macos-27-golden-gate/">support macOS 27</a>, and Rogue Amoeba says Golden Gate <a href="https://weblog.rogueamoeba.com/2026/09/24/macos-27-fixes-multiple-audio-bugs/">fixes several long-standing problems</a> in the Mac&#8217;s audio system. Good news all around.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Happy birthday, Rogue Amoeba. Here&#8217;s to 24 more.</p>



